{
 "ios-actions|Menus": {
  "summary": "A Plenix menu on iOS is the system Menu (UIMenu), kept native in behavior (the press or tap that opens it, the morph from its button, VoiceOver, keyboard navigation on iPad) with Plenix deciding its content: short verb labels, sections in place of long lists, one submenu level, checkmarks for toggles and destructive items last. The system draws the menu surface, so its glass material, radius and SF Pro text stay Apple’s; where Plenix draws a menu itself, such as a custom popover list, it uses the Plenix menu tokens shown in the Plenix rows: an overlay surface with an 8-point radius and a 1-point border, 44-point rows, DM Sans labels and the Plenix danger and disabled colors.",
